The test passes two `DataArray` objects with identical coordinates into `xr.align(..., join="exact", copy=False)`. In this repository, `xr.align` comes from `xarray.structure.alignment`, and `Aligner.align()` ends with a three-way branch: `override` calls `override_indexes()`, `join == "exact" and not copy` assigns `self.results = self.objects`, and only the remaining case calls `self.reindex_all()`. Since the test uses `join="exact"` and `copy=False`, it takes the direct-results branch, so `reindex_all` is never invoked.

